      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The straight-line method for depreciation is a straightforward process. To calculate it, you'll need to determine the annual depreciation amount. \n\nYou can use the formula: Annual Depreciation = (Cost - Salvage Value) / Useful Life. In your case, that's (45,000 - 5,000) / 8. \n\nAnnual Depreciation = 40,000 / 8 = 5,000. \n\nNow, to find the total depreciation over the 8 years, you multiply the annual depreciation by the number of years: 5,000 * 8 = 40,000. \n\nSo, the total depreciation is $40,000. You can then subtract this from the original cost to find the book value after 8 years: 45,000 - 40,000 = 5,000. \n\nThis is a bit like how a well-organized group of goblins might work together to gather resources - each year, they chip away at the original cost, leaving behind a smaller, more manageable amount.",
